# Vault sync on commit + push

**When:** You create a git commit **and** publish it (`git push` / open PR that ships work).  
**What:** Update the Obsidian vault so docs match what was shipped.  
**Where:** `C:\Users\Kosov\OneDrive\Documents\ObsidianVaults\CodingProjekt1\CodingProjekt`

## Minimum updates

1. **`90 Changelog.md`** — dated entry (what shipped, commit/PR if useful).
2. **Affected notes** — e.g. `21 Codebase — Ko-Stream.md`, `10 Project.md`, `00 Start.md`, agent notes under `30 Agents/`, or Research/Reviews under `70 Documentation/` when relevant.

## Rules of thumb

- Commit alone without push → vault update optional; **commit + push → vault update required**.
- Prefer updating the vault in the same turn as the push (or hand off to `@cp1-documenter` / Documenter with the changelog facts).
- Do not leave the vault behind shipped `main` / published work.
- Vault path and agent roster: see `AGENTS.md` and vault `30 Agents.md`.
